 from  the National Crime Agency on fire a fire  and explosive expert gas and structural  expert and indeed an archaeologist we  have 15 more people coming to the island  on the 18th to help us again with DVI  and CSI crime investigation  advisors from the National Crime agency  in total 48 Specialists are supporting  what is an enormous operation and  investigation  forces from gloucestershire even in  Somerset Devon and Cornwall Dorset  Wiltshire and of course our close  friends in Guernsey and I've already  mentioned the National Crime agency as  well as help from specialist commercial  companies here in Jersey and the  National Police coordination Center for  which I am  enormously grateful  from an investigative point of view as I  announced earlier this week detective  superintendent Alan Fosse who is the  head of crime for states of Jersey  police will lead the investigation  currently with 20 full-time  investigators and an array of support  which I have just alluded to and listed  to support her with support from the UK  the investigation will be long  and it is complex  it will take weeks indeed it it will  take months  I fully appreciate  that families and friends of the victims  and our wider Community as a whole will  want to know and understand  how this tragic event occurred  we will get to that stage I promise  but it will take time  so I'm now asking for a degree of  patience as we begin to undertake a  detailed and meticulous professional  investigation  which will include the identification  and of course the inquests that the  families effective affected truly  deserve  thank you ladies and gentlemen I'll now  hand over to Paul Brown  thank you Robin  I too would like to Echo the comments of  the chief officer of the state of Jersey  police and and send our thoughts to the  families and friends of those who have  lost loved ones  I'd also like to thank Islanders for  their enduring strength and cooperation  over the last week  I visited the scene