 provide  command support and medical support for  those working on scene  in the days following the incident the  hospital received three people  one person from the scene remains in  their care  a special thanks needs to go to our  colleagues in health and Community  Services who have responded to the  incident at the weekend and who continue  to support  and offer support throughout  I would also like to take this  opportunity to explicitly thank the  agencies that have offered and provided  tremendous support to us throughout the  last five days  those include my own team within the  states of Jersey Ambulance Service  ambulance services from Southwest West  Midlands  Guernsey London  and the support that we've received from  the Coast Guard  NHS England  the national ambulance coordination  Center  St John Ambulance  Normandy rescue  and the Jersey ambulance support unit  I would like to thank Islanders for the  ongoing Corporation throughout the last  five days we are returning to business  as usual and Islanders can contact us  through the usual lines  thank you  thank you Pete thank you Paul we're now  available for questions  foreign  from BBC Channel Islands news  um on Saturday uh the first press  conference you said up to a do you  expected that up to a dozen were missing  and part of the reason behind that was  you were unsure about whether people  were visiting the flats that evening  um you've now said you there's no one  left unaccounted for is there a chance  you could potentially find further  fatalities of you has any light been  shed on whether there were visitors to  the hodamore flats that evening thanks  Amaya it's a really good question you  you will understand of course back on  Saturday the importance of caution uh  numbers are very important and the  sensitivity is attached to that  uh shortly after that we were working on  on nine fatalities we do not believe  there is anyone else but we we have  certain other things that we need to do  b